# [ONSEN](../wg/onsen.html)

## Summary

The ONSEN (Open Network Services Evolution and Maintenance) Working Group met during IETF 127. The session focused on refining the WG problem statement, structuring draft mapping across problem buckets, reviewing progress on service model extensions and TM Forum API interworking, discussing architectural frameworks for YANG orchestration and off-box device mapping, and reviewing open-source validation tooling and telco-cloud abstractions.

Key outcomes included agreement to proceed with a Call for Adoption for the ONSEN Problem Statement draft, consensus on splitting dynamic service scheduling and observability into standalone drafts, and moving the IETF device-to-vendor model mapping experiment work into ONSEN.

