### Extensions to the YANG Data Model for L3VPN Service Delivery
* **Presented by:** Fengchao Fu
* **Slides:** [5) Extensions to the YANG Data Model for L3VPN Service Delivery](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-onsen-slides-127-onsen-extensions-to-the-yang-data-model-for-l3vpn-service-delivery-00)
* **Overview:**
  * `draft-fu-onsen-update-l3sm` is being refactored to focus on scheduled service operations / dynamic VPN capabilities.
  * Proposed modeling approach reuses schedules from RFC 9922 using `choice` structures for one-shot execution (start/end time) and daily recurrence with timezone support.
  * Elastic bandwidth configuration is supported for L3VPN.
  * The work will form a new standalone draft providing reusable dynamic YANG groupings across both L2/L3 service models (SM) and network models (NM).
* **Discussion:**
  * **Mahesh Jethanandani** noted that the draft target should be Standards Track rather than Informational. He also requested clarification regarding references to RFC 9417 (SAIN). The author confirmed performance monitoring content related to RFC 9417 is being deferred to the separate observability draft.

