### Mapping YANG Schemas and Instance Data to TM Forum Data Models and APIs
* **Presented by:** Kristian Larsson & Kris Lambrechts
* **Slides:** [6) Mapping YANG Schemas and Instance Data to TM Forum Data Models and APIs](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-onsen-mapping-yang-schemas-and-instance-data-to-tm-forum-data-models-and-apis-00)
* **Overview:**
  * `draft-lambrechts-onsen-tmf-yang-mapping` specifies a deterministic mapping between YANG schemas/instance data and TM Forum OpenAPI specifications (TMF633/TMF634 for catalog discovery; TMF640/TMF641 for service ordering).
  * Proof of concept implemented in the open-source *StratoWeave* orchestrator.
  * Recent draft updates include mapping nested YANG containers/lists into TMF features using composition relationships.
* **Discussion & Technical Constraints:**
  * **Wim Henderickx** and **Kristian Larsson** discussed structural mismatches and data loss when mapping YANG to TMF (e.g., complex YANG `must` constraints do not directly translate into TMF JSON schemas and must be validated/rejected operationally at request runtime).
  * Key identifiers are transitioning to UUID mappings to align with TMF expectations while maintaining statefulness.

