### Experiment: Mapping IETF Device YANG Models to Vendor Models
* **Presented by:** Kristian Larsson & Ian Farrer
* **Slides:** [9) An Experiment: Mapping IETF Device YANG Models to Vendors](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-onsen-9-an-experiment-mapping-ietf-device-yang-models-to-vendors-01)
* **Overview:**
  * Explores off-box compilation and translation from standard IETF device YANG models (BGP, IS-IS, Interfaces, Routing) to proprietary vendor native configurations (Cisco IOS-XR, Juniper Junos, Arista/ArcOS OpenConfig, Huawei VRP).
  * Validated during the IETF 127 Hackathon across four vendor platforms acting as MPLS LERs providing L3VPN services.
  * Work will formally transfer from the NMOP WG to ONSEN for future revisions.
* **Discussion:**
  * **Rob Wilson** noted vendors often perform similar translations on-box (e.g., OpenConfig to native). He highlighted edge cases including mixed native/standard configurations, default value handling, cross-referencing policy models, and propagating low-level execution errors back to high-level IETF model leaves.

